= The Chronicle Closes

Two years and more have passed since DuFour left the stage, and the Commonwealth has settled — however uneasily — into whatever it is now to become. The crises that defined the age have burned down to embers; the quarrels that remain belong to a different generation, and to a different chronicle than this one.

The story of the republic's hardest years is told. What the Marchers made of them — and what was made of the Marchers — is now a matter for the histories.

- @game_over_1934: Bring the era to a close.
